<h1>Daniel Biss</h1>
<p>US House, 9th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.danielbiss.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (danielbiss.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Biss&#39;s campaign site says his priorities are protecting communities, lowering costs and building a government that works for everyone, and his issues page lists restoring antitrust enforcement, strengthening workers&#39; right to organize, climate action, campaign finance reform and lowering housing, health care and child care costs. In his Sun-Times questionnaire he says he supports a national single-payer system such as Medicare for All, says ICE should be abolished, and backs a path to citizenship and a ban on stock trading by members of Congress. He also lists gun violence reduction, public school investment and protecting Social Security and Medicare.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Mayor of Evanston since 2021; previously served in the Illinois House and the Illinois Senate.</p>
